## ✨ Application Screens & Features

Traveloop consists of **14 comprehensive screens**, each designed to cover a specific stage of the travel planning journey.

<img src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/73097560/115834477-dbab4500-a447-11eb-908a-139a6edaec5c.gif" width="100%">

### 🔐 1. Login / Signup Screen

> **Entry point of the application** — allows users to securely create a new account or access their existing one.

**Purpose:** Authenticate users so they can manage their personal travel plans, saved trips, and preferences in a secure environment.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 📧 Email and password input fields with real-time validation
- 🔑 Login button and dedicated Signup link for new users
- 🔓 "Forgot Password" flow for account recovery
- ⚠️ Inline form validation with clear error messages (e.g., invalid email format, weak password)
- 📱 Responsive layout that adapts cleanly across desktop and mobile

---

### 🏠 2. Dashboard / Home Screen

> **Central hub of the application** — the first screen users see after logging in, providing a complete overview of their travel activity.

**Purpose:** Allows users to quickly navigate to their existing trips, discover new destinations, and take immediate action on planning new journeys.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 👋 Personalized welcome message with the user's name
- 🗂️ List of **recent and upcoming trips** displayed as summary cards
- ➕ Prominent **"Plan New Trip"** call-to-action button
- 🌍 **Recommended destinations** section with curated city suggestions and travel inspiration
- 💰 **Budget highlights** showing a quick snapshot of spending across active trips
- 🔔 Notification area for upcoming trip reminders or budget alerts

---

### ✏️ 3. Create Trip Screen

> **The starting point for any new journey** — a clean, intuitive form that collects all the essential details needed to kick off a trip plan.

**Purpose:** Begins the process of creating a personalized travel plan by capturing the core trip metadata before the user dives into itinerary building.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🏷️ **Trip Name** — a descriptive title for the journey
- 📅 **Start & End Dates** — interactive date picker to define the trip duration
- 📝 **Trip Description** — free-text field for notes, goals, or context about the trip
- 🖼️ **Cover Photo Upload** *(optional)* — dropzone to personalize the trip card with an image
- 💾 **Save Button** — creates the trip and redirects to the Itinerary Builder
- ✅ Field-level validation to ensure required information is filled before saving

---

### 📋 4. My Trips (Trip List) Screen

> **Personal trip management hub** — a complete list view of all trips the user has created, past or upcoming.

**Purpose:** Gives users a single, organized place to access, manage, and review all of their travel plans without needing to search or scroll through unrelated content.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🃏 **Trip Cards** displaying:
  - Trip name and cover photo
  - Travel date range (start → end)
  - Number of destinations/stops included
  - Current status (Draft / Active / Completed)
- ✏️ **Edit** button — opens the trip for modification
- 👁️ **View** button — opens the read-only Itinerary View
- 🗑️ **Delete** button — removes the trip with a confirmation prompt
- 🔍 Search and filter bar to sort trips by date or destination

---

### 🗺️ 5. Itinerary Builder Screen

> **The core planning workspace** — an interactive interface where users construct their full trip, stop by stop, day by day.

**Purpose:** Allows users to build a comprehensive, day-wise travel plan by adding cities, assigning travel dates, and filling each stop with activities in a fluid, drag-and-drop environment.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- ➕ **"Add Stop" Button** — adds a new city/destination to the itinerary
- 🏙️ **City Selector** — search and select cities to assign to each stop
- 📅 **Date Assignment** — define arrival and departure dates for each stop
- 🎯 **Activity Assignment** — browse and attach activities to specific days and stops
- 🔄 **Reorder Cities** — drag and drop stops to rearrange the order of the journey
- 📌 **Stop Summary** — each stop displays a collapsible summary of its days, activities, and estimated cost
- 💾 Auto-save functionality to prevent data loss during planning

---

### 📆 6. Itinerary View Screen

> **The read-only trip overview** — a polished, visual representation of the completed itinerary designed for reviewing and sharing.

**Purpose:** Lets users (and anyone they share with) review the full trip plan in a well-structured, easy-to-read format — without the ability to accidentally edit it.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🗓️ **Day-wise Layout** — each day is presented as a distinct section with its own timeline
- 🏙️ **City Headers** — clear labels indicating which city the day belongs to
- 🎯 **Activity Blocks** — individual cards for each activity showing:
  - Activity name and description
  - Scheduled time
  - Estimated cost
- 🔀 **View Mode Toggle** — switch between **Calendar View** (date-grid style) and **List View** (vertical timeline)
- 🖨️ Print/export-friendly layout for offline reference

---

### 🔎 7. City Search Screen

> **Destination discovery tool** — helps users find and research cities to include in their travel plans.

**Purpose:** Enables users to discover relevant cities with key travel information and seamlessly add them to their ongoing trip itinerary.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🔍 **Search Bar** — real-time city search with auto-suggestions
- 🌆 **City Result Cards** showing:
  - City name, country, and region
  - Popularity rating and travel highlights
  - Estimated cost index
- 📌 **"Add to Trip" Button** — instantly adds the city as a new stop in the active itinerary
- 🗂️ **Filters** — narrow results by country, region, or cost range
- 📖 Expandable city detail panel with brief descriptions and top activity previews

---

### 🎭 8. Activity Search Screen

> **Experience discovery engine** — helps users browse, research, and select things to do at each destination.

**Purpose:** Enriches the trip with curated experiences such as sightseeing tours, food experiences, adventure activities, cultural events, and more.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🏷️ **Activity Filters** — filter by:
  - **Type** (sightseeing, adventure, food, culture, relaxation)
  - **Cost** (budget-friendly to premium)
  - **Duration** (1 hour, half-day, full-day)
- 🃏 **Activity Cards** showing name, category, estimated cost, and duration
- 🖼️ **Quick View Panel** — tap/click for a detailed description, images, and traveler reviews
- ➕ **Add Button** — adds the activity directly to a selected stop in the itinerary
- ➖ **Remove Button** — removes a previously added activity
- 🔍 Keyword search for finding specific activities by name or interest

---

### 💰 9. Trip Budget & Cost Breakdown Screen

> **Financial intelligence dashboard** — a comprehensive view of the estimated costs for the entire trip, broken down intelligently.

**Purpose:** Helps travelers stay informed about their spending, plan more effectively, and avoid surprises by seeing exactly where their money is going.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🥧 **Pie / Donut Chart** — visual breakdown of costs by category:
  - 🚌 Transport
  - 🏨 Stay / Accommodation
  - 🎭 Activities
  - 🍽️ Meals
- 📊 **Bar Chart** — daily cost comparison across the entire trip duration
- 📈 **Average Cost Per Day** — automatically calculated and displayed
- 🔴 **Over-Budget Alerts** — highlighted warnings for days or categories that exceed the set budget
- 💵 **Total Estimated Cost** — sum of all planned expenses across all stops
- ✏️ Budget input field allowing users to set their overall trip budget for comparison

---

### 🎒 10. Packing Checklist Screen

> **Smart packing assistant** — a per-trip checklist that keeps travelers organized and ensures nothing important is forgotten.

**Purpose:** Helps travelers manage what they need to pack, track what's already been packed, and reuse the checklist across future trips.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- ➕ **Add Items** — type in custom items to add to the checklist
- ✅ **Mark as Packed** — check off items as they're packed with visual completion feedback
- 🗑️ **Remove Items** — delete items that are no longer needed
- 🗂️ **Category Organization** — group items by type:
  - 👕 Clothing
  - 📄 Documents
  - 💻 Electronics
  - 🧴 Toiletries
  - 💊 Medications
  - 🎁 Miscellaneous
- 📊 **Progress Bar** — shows the percentage of items packed at a glance
- 🔄 **Reset Checklist** — clear all checked items to reuse the list for another trip

---

### 🌐 11. Shared / Public Itinerary View Screen

> **Social sharing and inspiration hub** — a publicly accessible version of a user's itinerary that can be shared with anyone.

**Purpose:** Allows users to share their travel plans with friends, family, or the wider travel community — and lets others get inspired or even copy the trip for their own use.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 🔗 **Unique Public URL** — a shareable link that anyone can open without logging in
- 📋 **Itinerary Summary** — displays the full trip in a clean, read-only format
- 📑 **"Copy Trip" Button** — logged-in users can clone the shared itinerary into their own account
- 📣 **Social Media Sharing** — quick-share buttons for WhatsApp, Twitter/X, Facebook, and link copy
- 🔒 **Read-Only View** — visitors can browse but cannot modify the itinerary
- 👁️ View count display showing how many people have seen the itinerary

---

### 👤 12. User Profile / Settings Screen

> **Account management center** — where users control their personal information, preferences, and account settings.

**Purpose:** Enables users to keep their profile up to date, personalize their experience, and manage their account privacy and data.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- ✏️ **Editable Profile Fields:**
  - Full name
  - Profile photo (upload/change)
  - Email address
- 🌏 **Language Preference** — select the preferred display language
- 📌 **Saved Destinations List** — view and manage cities the user has bookmarked for future trips
- 🔐 **Change Password** — secure password update flow
- 🗑️ **Delete Account** — permanent account removal with a confirmation step and data warning
- 🔔 Notification preferences for trip reminders and budget alerts

---

### 📓 13. Trip Notes / Journal Screen

> **In-app travel journal** — a lightweight note-taking tool tied directly to trips and stops for contextual record-keeping.

**Purpose:** Lets travelers capture and organize important details — such as hotel check-in times, local contacts, confirmation numbers, or day-specific reminders — without ever leaving the app.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- ➕ **Add Note** — create a new note linked to a specific trip or a specific stop/day
- ✏️ **Edit Note** — update existing notes at any time
- 🗑️ **Delete Note** — remove notes that are no longer needed
- 🕒 **Timestamp Display** — each note shows when it was created or last modified
- 📋 **Notes List View** — sorted by date, with the most recent notes at the top
- 🔍 Search within notes to quickly find specific information

---

### 📊 14. Admin / Analytics Dashboard *(Optional — Must)*

> **Platform command center** — an admin-only interface for monitoring the health, usage, and growth of the Traveloop platform.

**Purpose:** Helps platform administrators track user behavior, identify popular content, and make data-driven decisions about the product's direction.

**Key Components & Functionality:**
- 📈 **Platform Overview Cards:**
  - Total trips created
  - Total active users
  - Trips shared publicly
  - New signups (daily/weekly/monthly)
- 🏙️ **Top Destinations Chart** — most frequently added cities across all trips
- 🎭 **Top Activities Chart** — most popular activities added by users
- 👥 **User Management Table** — list of all registered users with basic account details and status
- 📉 **User Engagement Stats** — session frequency, feature usage, and retention metrics
- 🗑️ Admin controls to suspend or remove user accounts if necessary

<img src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/73097560/115834477-dbab4500-a447-11eb-908a-139a6edaec5c.gif" width="100%">

